bstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The beat-unit-tied type indicates a beat-unit within a metronome mark that is tied to the preceding beat-unit."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This allows two or more tied notes to be associated with a per-minute value in a metronome mark, whereas the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome-tied element is restricted to metric relationship marks."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BeatUnitTied","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"MXLMetronome.BeatUnitTied","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BeatUnitTied","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLMetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLMetronome","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}]}}}